{"answer":"A customization interface is a set of methods for creating, managing, and using custom models to adapt a service’s behavior.

For IBM Watson Speech to Text, it lets you customize a base model for your domain and audio to improve speech recognition accuracy. It supports both custom language models and custom acoustic models; you use a model in a recognition request by specifying its customization ID. [S1][S2]

For speech synthesis, the interface lets you create and manage custom models containing word/translation pairs that tell the service how to pronounce words. [S4][S5]","abstain":false,"citations":["S1","S2","S4","S5"]}
